# Level 1-05: Either Door — an OR door needs only ONE of its plates held, unlike the
# AND door in 1-02/1-04. Plate B is a reachable, perfectly valid alternative that this
# solution simply doesn't need — proving "either" is enough.
#
# Trace (spine at x=3, spawn (3,0), goal (3,8), door (3,7)=door:or:a+b):
#   Branch to B: (3,4)-(2,4)-(1,4). Branch to A: (3,2)-(4,2)-(5,2). Both dead ends off
#   the spine, reachable by walking the spine to the junction row then stepping sideways.
#   Loop 1 (recorded): tick1 (3,0)->(3,1), tick2 ->(3,2), tick3 ->(4,2), tick4 ->(5,2)=A.
#     Plate A activates at tick4 -> Door.Recompute fires immediately -> door OR is open
#     from tick4 onward for the rest of this loop and every loop after (ghost idles on A
#     forever once its recording runs out). Loop then runs out its full LOOP_SECONDS timer
#     (World1 has no manual split) and a ghost is spawned holding A.
#   Loop 2 (final, live, unencumbered): ghost1 replays the tick1-4 path above and is back
#     on A by tick4 of this loop too, so the door is already open long before the player
#     gets there. Live player walks straight up the spine, never touching either plate:
#     tick1 (3,1), tick2 (3,2) [passes the A junction without turning], tick3 (3,3),
#     tick4 (3,4) [passes the B junction without turning], tick5 (3,5), tick6 (3,6),
#     tick7 (3,7)=door — door state checked is "as of start of tick7" = open since tick4,
#     so the player walks straight through, no bump — tick8 (3,8)=goal. Level complete at
#     tick8 of loop 2. Total: 2 loops, ~8 ticks in the solving loop.
#   Plate B is reachable too (spine to (3,4) then (2,4),(1,4)) but is never needed here —
#     that's the point of OR.
NAME: 1-05 Either Door
WORLD: 1
LOOP_SECONDS: 20
MAX_TIMELINES: 1
PAR_LOOPS: 2
PAR_TICKS: 12
GRID:
###G###
###D###
###.###
###.###
#B..###
###.###
###..A#
###.###
###S###
LEGEND:
S=spawn G=goal A=plate:a B=plate:b D=door:or:a+b
